  <main_text>
    <l n="1" type="heading" level="1" para="true">Illustrissimo &amp; Nobilissimo Viro</l>
    <l n="2" type="heading" level="1">DOMINO D.</l>
    <l n="3" type="heading" level="1">JOSEPHO WILLIAMSON</l>
    <l n="4" type="heading" level="1">EQUITI AURATO,</l>
    <l n="5" type="heading" level="1">REGI</l>
    <l n="6" type="heading" level="1">ABOMNIBUS CONSILIIS ET SECRETIS</l>
    <l n="7" type="heading" level="1">REGIÆ SCIENTIARUM SOCIETATIS</l>
    <l n="8" type="heading" level="1">PRÆSIDI NERITISSIMO,</l>
    <l n="9" type="heading" level="1">INGENIO PRÆSTANTI, ET ERUDITIONE PERFECTA</l>
    <l n="10" type="heading" level="1">ORNATO,</l>
    <l n="11" type="heading" level="1">JUDICIO ACRI, ET MEMORIA ADMIRABILI</l>
    <l n="12" type="heading" level="1">PRÆDITO,</l>
    <l n="13" type="heading" level="1">INDUSTRIA IN AGENDO, CONSILIO IN PROVIDENDO</l>
    <l n="14" type="heading" level="1">UT STUDIO ET FIDELITATE IN</l>
    <l n="15" type="heading" level="1">RELIGIONEM, REGEM, REMPUBLICAM</l>
    <l n="16" type="heading" level="1">NULLI SECUNDO,</l>
    <l n="17" type="heading" level="1">SUMMO LITERATORUM FAUTORI,</l>
    <l n="18" type="heading" level="1">LITERARUM SCIENTIÆ ET</l>
    <l n="19" type="heading" level="1">ELOQUENDI ELEGANTIÆ,</l>
    <l n="20" type="heading" level="1">AMPLIFICATORI</l>
    <l n="21" para="true">Hoc qualecunque opusculum dicat, vovet,</l>
    <l n="22">ac consecrat inprimis addictus, deditus,</l>
    <l n="23">&amp; obstrictus</l>
    <l n="24" para="true">Carolus Maria de Veïl</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>The dedication is set in mixed roman, italic, small capitals and display sizes; the headline is rendered as one head, with the display lines run together. The signature "Carolus Maria de Veïl" is in italic, set right-aligned. Some letters in the scan are damaged (e.g. "Hoc qualecunque opusculum", "addictus", "obstrictus" with worn letters), but the readings are clear enough. A small mark is visible at the bottom left of the page, not transcribed.</notes>
